---
const pageTitle = "nyxbug404 | About";
---

<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>{pageTitle}</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>

<body>
    <header>
        <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back to Hub</a>
        <span style="font-weight: 600; color: #888;">nyxbug404 Creator</span>
    </header>

    <div class="page-shell">
        <aside class="sidebar">
            <div class="sidebar-title">Explore</div>
            <a href="/adults">Adults</a>
            <a href="/kids">Kids</a>
        </aside>
        <main>
            <section class="hero-section">
                <h1>About the Creator</h1>
            </section>

            <section style="margin-top: 1rem; line-height: 1.6;">
                <p class="section-desc" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    Welcome to the chaos! If you are wondering who is behind all of this, hi, I am a late-diagnosed ADHD
                    and ASD mom, and I am just trying to figure it all out. Between managing a full-time regular day job
                    and everyday life, I squeeze in this content creation wherever I can find the time, building things
                    for myself and the boys as I learn more about my own neurodivergence.
                </p>
                <p class="section-desc" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    We are mostly creating this stuff for ourselves, and I am honestly just hoping that others might be
                    interested and want it too. Thank you so much for your patience as I learn these new skills and try
                    to stay focused on one project at a time instead of jumping around like a pinball.
                </p>
                <p class="section-desc" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    By the way, if you see anything labeled as "coming soon" around here, it's just there to show you
                    what I'm planning. Honestly, to keep me from totally forgetting what I'm supposed to be working on
                    next! It just means I'm either finding the time to tackle it or figuring out the software skills as
                    I go.
                </p>
                <p class="section-desc" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    Most of the time, I get completely lost in a screen working on these projects and lose track of
                    time, forgetting to eat entirely until food magically appears by my side from my thoughtful husband,
                    or until he stages an intervention to rescue me from the screen and help get the kids to bed. The inspiration for all of this
                    comes from my boys, random daily activities, or whatever video game I am obsessing over at the
                    moment.
                </p>
                <p class="section-desc" style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    I make a conscious effort to keep the designs simple to prevent overwhelm and unnecessary
                    distractions, which is good because my brain already wants to go in a million directions at once. I
                    am always having to catch myself as I drift off task or go down ridiculous rabbit holes, constantly
                    telling myself to focus and get back to the actual project.
                </p>
                <p class="section-desc" style="margin-bottom: 3em;">
                    At the end of the day, I am just having fun building things I love, and I am so glad you stopped by
                    to check them out.
                </p>
                <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; width: 100%; margin-top: 2rem;">
                    <a href="/" class="image-button"
                        style="background-image: url('/images/nyxbug404 Website Busy Desk.png');" title="Back to Home">
                    </a>
                </div>
            </section>

        </main>

    </div>


</body>

</html>